            <ArticleTitle>[Electrolyte metabolism in thyrotoxicosis with energy-dynamic cardiac insufficiency].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>7-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In 70 patients with thyrotoxicosis and in 24--with ischemic heart disease with energy-dynamic cardiac insufficiency a study was made of electrolyte metabolism in the blood plasma, erythrocytes and 24-hour urine. The sodium and potassium content in erythrocytes rose, and sodium gradient diminished in the patients examined, this being related to the development of energy-dynamic cardiac insufficiency.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
